ALVA — Portrait Mode & Slide Controls Update

Mission

Implement full portrait-orientation support for Alva, introducing a new gameplay input system named Slide Controls.

Alva must become a truly dual-orientation mobile game, not simply a landscape game compressed into a vertical screen.

The guiding principle:

Alva should feel as natural to play with one or two fingers in portrait as it does with a controller in landscape. Players should perform actions according to what they visually expect their fighter to do, without needing to memorize arbitrary inputs.

This is a major gameplay input and interface update. Implement it as a complete, production-ready feature using Alva’s existing architecture.

Do not rebuild combat mechanics, alter character balance, or compromise the existing landscape experience.

