2. Two mobile experiences

Alva will support two complete mobile experiences determined automatically by device orientation.

Landscape — Original Alva

Landscape must remain essentially unchanged.

Retain:

* Joystick controls
* Classic Buttons controls
* Existing touch control customization
* Existing controller and keyboard support
* Existing battle interface
* Existing fighter ability artwork and button indicators

Do not remove existing customization, reset saved layouts, or change gameplay rules.

Portrait — Slide Controls

Portrait automatically activates the new Slide Controls system.

There must be:

* No virtual joystick
* No attack buttons
* No jump button
* No movement buttons
* No Shield button
* No Dash button
* No invisible conventional button overlay masquerading as gestures

The game screen itself becomes the control surface.

The player interacts directly with the battlefield using taps, holds, and swipes.

Normal interface controls such as Pause, Back, Settings, and menu choices remain available when appropriate. The buttonless requirement concerns gameplay actions, not the ability to navigate the game.

Orientation transitions

When a player rotates the device:

Landscape to portrait

* Disable conventional mobile gameplay controls.
* Clear their held input state.
* Activate Slide Controls.
* Recalculate the battlefield and interface layout.
* Preserve the ongoing battle.

Portrait to landscape

* Release all active gestures and associated gameplay inputs.
* Disable Slide Controls.
* Restore the selected landscape control layout.
* Recalculate the camera and interface.
* Preserve the ongoing battle.

Never interpret orientation-change touch events as gameplay commands.

Do not restart a fight, reset the match timer, replenish resources, or change the player’s selected fighter.

Existing orientation changes automatically pause the game in some situations. Remove that portrait restriction carefully. Orientation changes must not create an unintended pause; an already paused game should remain paused.

Portrait support applies only to mobile/touch-capable devices. Do not classify a desktop as mobile merely because its browser window is narrow.

